---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import UnreleasedNotice from '../../../components/reference/UnreleasedNotice.astro';
import { loadExport } from '../../../data/export';

const { telemetry } = loadExport();
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Usage reporting',
		description:
			'Every field of the daily anonymous report a FoxAuth server sends, and how to turn it off.'
	}}
>
	<UnreleasedNotice />
	<p>
		Once a day, a FoxAuth server sends one small report to the FoxAuth maintainers. The report says which
		version the server runs, on what, with which features on, and roughly how big it is. The maintainers
		use it to decide what to keep, what to fix first and what nobody uses any more.
	</p>
	<p>
		Reporting is on by default. Nothing in a report names you, your projects, your applications or your
		users. A report that cannot be delivered is not an error: the server carries on and tries again the
		next day.
	</p>

	<h2>Turning it off</h2>
	<p>
		In the console: <strong>Settings → Integrations → Usage reporting</strong>. The change applies at
		once, without a restart. This setting is the only switch.
	</p>
	<p>
		The console card under the switch shows the exact report the server last sent, so you can check
		what left it.
	</p>
	<p>
		The addresses that attack a server are reported separately, hourly, under a switch of their own:
		see <a href="/docs/reference/attack-reports/">Attack reporting</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Where it goes</h2>
	<p>
		Reports go to <code>{telemetry.destination}</code>, run by the FoxAuth maintainers. The receiver does
		not store the address a report comes from, and keeps reports for 13 months.
	</p>

	<h2>Every field</h2>
	<p>
		This is format {telemetry.format}. Counts are never exact: each is sent as one of these ranges:{' '}
		{telemetry.rangeLabels.map((label, index) => (
			<>
				{index > 0 ? ', ' : ''}
				<code>{label}</code>
			</>
		))}.
	</p>
	<table>
		<thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>What it says</th><th>Values</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			{telemetry.fields.map((field) => (
				<tr>
					<td><code>{field.path}</code></td>
					<td>
						{field.meaning}
						{field.absentWhen ? <> Left out when {field.absentWhen}.</> : ''}
					</td>
					<td>{field.values}</td>
				</tr>
			))}
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2>Never sent</h2>
	<p>
		No name, email, hostname, issuer URL or network address. No identifier of a project, an application
		or a person. No value of any setting: only whether the features below are on or off.
	</p>

	<h2>Settings whose on/off is reported</h2>
	<ul>
		{telemetry.reportedSettings.map((setting) => (
			<li><a href={`/docs/reference/settings/#${setting.key}`}><code>{setting.key}</code></a>: {setting.label}</li>
		))}
	</ul>

	<h2>Settings that are not reported</h2>
	<ul>
		{telemetry.unreportedSettings.map((setting) => (
			<li><code>{setting.key}</code>: {setting.reason}.</li>
		))}
	</ul>
</StarlightPage>
